# Spotter RUNTIME STATE — per-machine, never shared.
# These were tracked. With two rigs sharing this repo (Windows + the Mac team)
# that is a live collision: both write every cycle, so both trees are
# permanently dirty and conflict on pull — and if either side commits, the
# other's spotter inherits a BYTE COUNT TAKEN FROM A DIFFERENT MACHINE'S LOG.
# spot.sh tracks progress by comparing that count to the local file size, so an
# inherited number makes it read a bogus delta or go silently blind. A git pull
# should never be able to blind the monitor.
scripts/spotter/last-size.txt
scripts/spotter/quiet-count.txt
scripts/spotter/spotter-alert.txt
scripts/spotter/spotter-status.log
